extends RefCounted

# Alternative soundtrack: 5 candidate tracks for every place music plays, so Matthew can
# audition them in Options > Soundtrack and pick one per slot (0 = keep the original).
# Each entry is a GenesisMusic song dictionary (see SONG_DEFAULTS in genesis_music.gd):
#   "style"  groove / rhythm section. 0-8 are the original stage grooves; the extras are
#            9 chiptune, 10 drum & bass, 11 outrun, 12 orchestral (gv 0 march, gv 1 taiko),
#            13 ambient, 14 lo-fi boom-bap, 15 bossa nova, 16 industrial, 17 6/8 ballad.
#   "bass" / "pad" / "arp" / "lead"  instrument voices (default: the groove's own).
#            bass: 0 picked rock, 1 slap FM, 2 fretless, 3 sine sub, 5 acid saw, 7 pumping saw,
#                  9 8-bit triangle, 10 reese, 11 FM keyboard bass, 12 low strings, 13 808, 14 upright
#            pad:  0 brass, 1 clavinet stabs, 2 flute organ / choir, 3 soft sine, 5 saw, 6 Rhodes,
#                  7 gated hypersaw, 8 analog saw, 9 8-bit pulse, 10 strings, 11 drawbar organ,
#                  12 warm analog pad, 13 strummed guitar
#            arp:  2 harp, 3 marimba, 4 ice bell, 6 sonar, 8 pulse pluck, 9 8-bit pulse,
#                  10 vibraphone, 11 steel drum, 12 nylon guitar
#            lead: 0 hollow square, 1 sync square, 2 bell flute, 3 pan flute, 4 glass bell,
#                  5 overdriven guitar, 6 sine bell, 7 supersaw, 9 8-bit pulse, 10 PWM synth,
#                  11 brass, 12 violin, 13 whistle, 14 FM electric piano
#   "prog_a" / "prog_b"  8 bars of chord roots as scale degrees (0 = home chord, negative = below).
#   Melodies are composed from "seed" (see GenesisMusic.compose_melody): "density" 0 long
#   notes / 1 medium / 2 busy, "mel_lo".."mel_hi" the verse range in scale degrees, and the
#   chorus sits "lift" degrees higher. A candidate can instead spell out "mel_a" / "mel_b".
#   "kit" picks a drum tuning from KITS.
# Hyperspace entries ("hyper") are ~2.6 s jingles: lists indexed by 16th step from the jump.

